  "content": {
    "title": "When is Selection Sunday for March Madness 2026? Time, channel for bracket reveal",
    "text": "Updated March 15, 2026, 9:18 a.m. ETThe NCAA Tournament is nearly here.The Akron Zips will be be part of March madness for third year in a row, and the fourth time in five years. Akron earned an automatic bid to the NCAA Tournament after coming back to beat Toledo in the Mid-American Conference tournament championship on Saturday night.Now the Zips have to wait to find out who they'll play this year. Here's how to watch the NCAA Tournament bracket release today:When is Selection Sunday?Date: Sunday, March 15Selection Sunday is set to take place on Sunday, March 15, for the men's NCAA Tournament.What time is selection show on TV for March Madness today?The selection show bracket reveal begins at 6 p.m. ET.What channel is selection show on Sunday for March Madness bracket?TV channel: CBSStreaming option: Fubo (free trial)When does March Madness start in 2026? Here's the NCAA Tournament scheduleThe opening games, known as the First Four, are scheduled for March 17 and March 18 in Dayton, Ohio.The full schedule includes:Selection Sunday: March 15First Four: March 17–18First round: March 19–20Second round: March 21–22Sweet 16: March 26–27Elite Eight: March 28–29Final Four: April 4National championship: April 6The Final Four and championship game will be played at Lucas Oil Stadium in Indianapolis.Who won the NCAA Tournament last year?The Florida Gators won the 2025 NCAA men’s basketball championship.Florida defeated the Houston Cougars 65–63 in the national championship game on April 7, 2025, in San Antonio.The win gave Florida its third national title and its first since winning back-to-back championships in 2006 and 2007.How many teams make the NCAA Tournament?The men’s NCAA Tournament features 68 teams.Thirty-one teams earn automatic bids by winning their conference tournaments. The remaining spots are filled with at-large selections chosen by the NCAA selection committee.Four games in the First Four round determine the final teams that advance into the traditional 64-team bracket for the first round.Where the First Four games are played in the NCAA TournamentThe First Four games are held each year at UD Arena in Dayton, Ohio, which serves as the tournament’s opening site.Those games feature the lowest-seeded automatic qualifiers and the last at-large teams selected for the field. The winners move on to the first round later that week.Where is the Final Four 2026 taking place?The Final Four and championship games will be played at Lucas Oil Stadium in Indianapolis.",
